    {
      "kind": "group",
      "parts": ["min", "max", "notmin", "andlo", "andhi", "either", "scale"],
      "text": "Anti windup",
      "color": "magenta"
    },
    {
      "kind": "md",
      "body": "**Working principle.** SCALE starts at 1. If the integral is below MIN and the error is still negative, or above MAX and the error is still positive, SCALE drops to 0 and the [[part:Accumulator]] stops taking input. MIN and MAX are not hard limits -- the integral can drift a little past them -- but this is good enough for most ships.\n\nThe [[part:Accumulator]] must be in **Pulse** mode, clocked by the Reset_Clock channel, or it races.\n\nTune the two thresholds and the I constant for your ship."
    }
  ]
